CARD: SKIP / ACT I · THE WONDER · CHAPTER 01 / The Beginning / High in the Vell cirque, the ice has been here for longer than anyone has had a name for it. / This summer, it moves. / Go where the ground takes you. The river will follow. / LETTER · JULY 1962 / Postcard from Vell Foot / Dear Ma, the glacier comes right down to the top of the valley, blue as a gas flame, and at night you can hear it creak like a ship. The man at the inn says it was here before there were people to look at it. We swam (briefly!!). Tell Dad the fishing is useless and the view is not. Back Sunday. Love, J. / HOW STORY MODE SCORES / Steer the thaw / You are a block of glacier ice on its way to the sea. Steer left and right; gravity does the rest. The river forms behind you, exactly where you went. / Destruction scores / In Story Mode every structure you bring down scores points. Fences, cars, cottages, bridges: if it breaks, it counts. / The bigger the harm, the bigger the score / Structures are worth more the more damage they could do to the land and the people around them if they failed. A fence is worth little. A pipeline, an oil rig or a tall apartment block is worth the most. Aim for them. / Reach the sea / Every river ends at the sea. You melt as you go, so smooth lines keep more ice. Get there with some to spare. / Destruction points per structure. The more harm a structure can do to the land, water and people when it fails, the more it is worth. / STRUCTURE	POINTS / Oil rig	1,000 / Dam	900 / Pipel
